SQL Query Generator

-> You are writing an ORM (Object-Relational Mapper) library. You need to construct
   complex SQL query strings (e.g., SELECT ... FROM ... WHERE ... ORDER BY ...).
   Passing all these optional parameters into a single constructor would result in a ]
   massive, unreadable, and error-prone "telescoping constructor" (a constructor with 10+
   arguments, most of which might be null).

-> Task: Separate the construction of the complex query from its representation.
1. Create a QueryBuilder class with methods for each SQL clause (e.g., select(), from(), where(), orderBy()).
2. Ensure these methods return the builder instance itself (this) to allow method chaining
    (e.g., builder.select("id").from("users").build()).
3. Include a build() method that validates the inputs and returns the final generated SQL string.